---
// Pricing (site-prelaunch.md §3) — copy verbatim from "Page: Pricing" (#41, FINAL).
// Monthly-only: no annual figures landed, so the designed billing toggle ships dormant
// (NOT built — zero JS, per the design's own conditional + PM annual-pricing decision).
// Connection-optional: works with or without a broker connection. Core's $49 is the
// Accepted price (pricing-artifact.md §1, human sign-off 2026-06-30), matching
// FastSpring's catalog exactly. Tier symmetry is a compliance feature (spec §6.2):
// never differentiate.
// Free card (2026-07-22, stock-analyst-platform#1307): shipped decoupled from the
// trial-launch reveal (consult 0182, ADR 0145 item 6) — Free needs neither ORATS (#97)
// nor a live checkout, so it shipped alone, ahead of its CTA.
// CTAs lit (2026-08-22, stock-analyst-platform#2513/#2514) — BOTH cards, one change,
// because §6.2 makes a CTA on one card and none on the other the asymmetry the rule
// exists to prevent. This REPLACES this comment's own previous claim that "the chooser
// block and Core's trial CTA stay gated on #97/#31": both halves of that gate are dead.
// #31 closed `not_planned` (the pre-Dodo MoR application), and ADR 0560 item 3 superseded
// the #97 half on 2026-08-02 — "The Core trial offer is un-gated from ORATS… Core is
// offered at go-live" — because structure math is broker-fed, not vendor-fed. What
// actually gated the CTAs was live MoR checkout (#1459/#201/#1458, all closed) and the
// Core card's own unserved-layer claim (#2519, closed 2026-08-22).
// The chooser block remains unbuilt — it is separate copy, not part of #2513/#2514.
// Labels differ per site-copy-twiceover.md §Pricing (signed off); the CTA *treatment* is
// identical, which is what §6.2 and site-prelaunch.md §3's "equal weight" govern.
// Core's two sub-lines are the negative-option disclosure (ADR 0145, FTC/EU-UK
// auto-renewal) — verbatim, legal-flagged; they are not decoration and never ship
// without the CTA they qualify, nor it without them.
// Trimmed from the #1307 canonical draft (human direction 2026-07-22), then restored
// (2026-08-22, stock-analyst-platform#2567): "— ongoing, not a trial" and the standalone
// "No card required" line were dropped as redundant on a card with no CTA/checkout to
// contrast against. #2513/#2514 falsified that premise by adding one — both lines now
// have exactly the contrast they were dropped for lacking (Free is "ongoing, not a
// trial" beside a 14-day trial; "No card required" beside a card-required CTA) — and
// the PM's site-copy-twiceover.md re-derivation (routed from #2544) ratified restoring
// them as part of the same pass that added the Sector/Voices/news-wire bullets below.
// "Any ticker" → "any US-listed
// ticker" per consult 0416 (PM ruling): the product is US-only by design (ADR
// 0027/0028) and US-venue-scoped by construction; inline qualifier, not a footnote,
// to preserve tier-card symmetry (spec §6.2).
// Premium card removed (2026-08-02, stock-analyst-platform#1766/#1767): realizes
// pricing-artifact.md's go-live gate (human direction, 2026-07-22) — while #1304
// (live analyst research) is open, Premium is held out of checkout/pricing entirely
// (hidden, not offered), matching the in-app Plans page's Free/Core state. Re-add
// trigger: when #1304 and the deferred-layers.lit flip both close, re-add as its own
// copy PR (content preserved in site-copy-twiceover.md's git history pre-2026-08-02).
// Core card's options/research bullets narrowed (2026-08-22, stock-analyst-platform#2519,
// ADR 0741): "Licensed market and options data" and "...and the research layer" claimed
// two layers served on no tier (options-iv/options-chain/flow dark per ADR 0560 item 1;
// analyst research Core "—" per pricing-artifact.md §3) on a page public+indexed since
// 2026-07-21. Narrowed to what's actually served; re-add each half as its own bullet
// when that layer ships and is licensed (site-copy-twiceover.md §Pricing has the ruling).
// Free/Core bullets re-derived against live production flag state (2026-08-22,
// stock-analyst-platform#2544/#2567): both cards omitted three things the product
// already serves live. Sector regime & peer positioning (always-on, no tier gate —
// layers.ts's `sector` carries no LAYER_MIN_TIER entry, #1233) belongs on both cards;
// curated voices and the licensed news wire are Core-minimum entitlements
// (LAYER_MIN_TIER: { voices: 'core', news: 'core' }) that were never listed on Core at
// all — voices.lit retired (#2064), so "coming soon" no longer applies. Options
// analytics stays correctly absent from both cards — that layer is still dark
// (DEFERRED_LAYERS, ADR 0560).
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

// Offer JSON-LD (SEO audit 2026-07 finding 7) — the Accepted prices, verbatim from
// pricing-artifact.md §1 (human sign-off 2026-06-30). No numbers invented here.
// Premium omitted (#1766/#1767) — the go-live gate holds it out of pricing entirely;
// a structured-data Offer is as much an advertisement of it as the visible card.
// url/availability/per-offer url (SEO re-audit 2026-08-23, stock-analyst-platform#2634): the site is
// trailingSlash: "never", so the old "/pricing/" 307-redirected to the real canonical — dropped the
// trailing slash. Each offer now also carries its own url (the live CTA it's actually redeemed
// through, already on the page below) and availability, per Google's Offer recommendations.
const productJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Product",
  name: "TwiceOver",
  url: "https://twiceover.io/pricing",
  offers: [
    {
      "@type": "Offer",
      name: "Free",
      price: "0",
      priceCurrency: "USD",
      availability: "https://schema.org/InStock",
      url: "https://twiceover.io/go/try",
    },
    {
      "@type": "Offer",
      name: "Core",
      price: "49",
      priceCurrency: "USD",
      availability: "https://schema.org/InStock",
      url: "https://twiceover.io/go/plan",
    },
  ],
};
---
<Base
  title="Pricing — TwiceOver"
  description="One simple monthly subscription. No per-analysis charges. Use it with or without a broker connection."
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(productJsonLd)} />
  <div class="page-title-block">
    <h1 class="type-heading-1">Simple subscription. You hold the decisions; we do the math.</h1>
    <p class="sub">One simple monthly subscription. No per-analysis charges. Use it with or without a broker connection — connecting read-only unlocks reads of your own positions against your own rules.</p>
  </div>

  <ul class="tier-grid">
    <li class="tier">
      <h2 class="type-heading-2">Free</h2>
      <p class="price type-display">$0</p>
      <ul>
        <li>15 reads a month — ongoing, not a trial</li>
        <li>The synthesis read on any US-listed ticker</li>
        <li>Key technical levels (basic), macro and sector regime, peer positioning, and SEC/EDGAR fundamentals</li>
        <li>No card required</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="btn-quiet tier__cta" href="/go/try">Run a free read</a>
    </li>
    <li class="tier">
      <h2 class="type-heading-2">Core</h2>
      <p class="price type-display">$49<span class="per">/mo</span></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Read-only broker connection</li>
        <li>Held-position reads and new-idea reads</li>
        <li>Options math &amp; structure engine (breakevens, max profit/loss, collateral, P&amp;L)</li>
        <li>Your own rules, evaluated on live data</li>
        <li>Macro and sector regime, with peer positioning</li>
        <li>Curated voices, plus the licensed news wire</li>
        <li>Licensed market data</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="btn-quiet tier__cta" href="/go/plan">Start 14-day trial</a>
      <p class="tier__disclosure">Free for 14 days. Then $49/month, charged automatically to the card you save at checkout.</p>
      <p class="tier__disclosure">Cancel any time before the trial ends — one click in Settings, no charge. We email you three days before.</p>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p class="mor-line">Subscriptions are sold by <strong>Dodo Payments</strong>, our merchant of record; TwiceOver is the software and service you're using. Prices in USD. You can cancel anytime; see the <a href="/refunds">Refund Policy</a>.</p>
</Base>
